# BMad's setup.py compares byte hashes of the vendored scripts in .claude/skills/*/scripts
# against their copies in _bmad/; a CRLF rewrite on checkout makes it report "stale" with
# no real change. Keep the BMad runtime files LF on every platform.
*.py   text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf

# The index is LF; keep every text file LF in the working tree too, so
# wp-scripts lint-js (prettier) sees the same endings on Windows and in CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored third-party code (the Freemius SDK, story 44) is committed byte for
# byte as its tagged release ships it, CRLF files included: no normalization.
post-quality-manager/vendor/** -text
